WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.650
- So wait, you have a two year old now?

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:02.483
- I do.

00:00:02.483 --> 00:00:03.899
- So how is that?
- Amazing.

00:00:03.899 --> 00:00:04.732
- Are you exhausted?

00:00:04.732 --> 00:00:05.565
Or you love it?

00:00:05.565 --> 00:00:06.398
- I love it.

00:00:06.398 --> 00:00:07.410
- You love every minute?
- I mean I,

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.810
I feel like it's the best thing that I've,

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.250
well, it is, I don't feel like it,

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.137
I know it's the best thing
I've ever done in my life,

00:00:13.137 --> 00:00:14.803
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- and yeah it's the most,

00:00:14.803 --> 00:00:15.720
it is really
- But wait two,

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.160
So like you don't have those
moments where you're like?

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.222
(Kelly mimics mad chuckling)

00:00:19.222 --> 00:00:20.055
(Cameron laughs)

00:00:20.055 --> 00:00:22.770
- I don't, I feel like as
a parent, that's your job

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:25.290
is to just be like okay, so
what are you feeling here?

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.130
How is it?

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:26.963
There's something there.

00:00:26.963 --> 00:00:30.124
Kids are always just trying
to express a feeling,

00:00:30.124 --> 00:00:30.957
- [Kelly] Yes!

00:00:30.957 --> 00:00:31.790
- they're not actively trying to be bad.

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:32.623
They're just trying to-
- But when

00:00:32.623 --> 00:00:34.080
they can't communicate,
they get so frustrated.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:34.913
- [Cameron] Exactly,

00:00:34.913 --> 00:00:36.579
so what is it?
- Yeah. I do my mom checklist.

00:00:36.579 --> 00:00:37.534
Did she eat? Is she tired?

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:38.527
I'm like, what time is it?

00:00:38.527 --> 00:00:39.930
You know?
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.693
- When was the last time
she ate? When did she,

00:00:41.693 --> 00:00:42.630
you know, when is nap?

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:43.463
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:43.463 --> 00:00:45.360
- You know, and you
just kind of start there

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.970
and then you go, like, what just happened?

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:49.950
Is there something she's
trying to communicate to me?

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:53.160
And I just have, I feel like as a parent,

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:57.870
my job is to just help her
find the words to her emotions,

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.730
her experience, what she's going through,

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.370
and be able to help her identify that

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.240
and then move through it,

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:04.410
and what does she need from me

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:05.790
and what does she need from herself?

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.340
And is this something
- [Kelly] God you're like-

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.173
- she can take care of herself,

00:01:08.173 --> 00:01:09.390
that she can self soothe
- Can we like talk

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:10.540
every week or-
- [Cameron] Yeah!

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:11.832
(Cameron laughs)

00:01:11.832 --> 00:01:13.931
- Are you like naturally a patient person?

00:01:13.931 --> 00:01:17.070
- Look it, I think that
because I'm an older parent

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:20.610
and I've already, I really
worked hard to get a child,

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:21.443
it's not something

00:01:21.443 --> 00:01:22.331
that just happened to me-
- I'm not like a young parent!

00:01:22.331 --> 00:01:23.310
I'm like...

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.230
- I know, but you know, I think
it's just a different thing

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:27.930
when I've also been
able, I'm very fortunate,

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:30.032
to have been able to
take the time to do it,

00:01:30.032 --> 00:01:31.698
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- and be there with her.

00:01:31.698 --> 00:01:33.780
And that's like just the hugest blessing

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:34.950
that I've had, yeah.
- That's great though.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.140
You have like the most
amazing outlook on that.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.000
- It's challenging, but
you know what's also

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.200
really imperative is to repair, you know?

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.240
Like if you do break, like blow up,

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.990
just to repair that and say,
oh my God, mommy lost (beep).

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.188
- Oh, that's what, yeah.

00:01:50.188 --> 00:01:51.021
(Cameron laughs)

00:01:51.021 --> 00:01:51.854
No, that's what,

00:01:51.854 --> 00:01:52.687
no that's what, yeah you do.
- And just like,

00:01:52.687 --> 00:01:54.210
I didn't mean to say that to you.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.043
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:55.043 --> 00:01:57.307
- If I hurt your feelings
or if I upset you,

00:01:57.307 --> 00:01:58.140
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:59.430
- I just want you to
know mommy's human too.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:01.096
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- You know what I mean?

00:02:01.096 --> 00:02:01.929
- I will say I'm lucky,

00:02:01.929 --> 00:02:04.050
my kids are very communicative
to me in that sense.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.587
Like, we're very open about...

00:02:05.587 --> 00:02:08.790
I'm not afraid to say,
oh man, mommy messed up,

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:09.623
- [Cameron] Yeah.

00:02:09.623 --> 00:02:10.456
- I should have handled it this way,

00:02:10.456 --> 00:02:12.630
but you know how sometimes
you get so frustrated

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.460
you don't, that happens
to mommy too, you know?

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:15.914
I was like, so we just need
to do better, so we do that,

00:02:15.914 --> 00:02:17.160
but it's...

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.930
You know what I think this
conversation deserves?

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:19.763
- [Cameron] What?

00:02:19.763 --> 00:02:20.596
- Some of your wine.

00:02:20.596 --> 00:02:21.429
- Okay!

00:02:21.429 --> 00:02:22.262
(audience applaud and cheer)

00:02:22.262 --> 00:02:23.095
(Cameron laughs)

00:02:23.095 --> 00:02:26.070
- [Kelly] I think that
we should have a drink!

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:26.910
- Cheers to you, mommy!

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.207
- [Kelly] To being a really great mom!

